    "findings":  [
                     "Portable executable: the window appears after about 51 s (self-extraction of the application and the 7,326-file runtime into a temporary folder on every launch); the engine is ready about 20 s later (verification of freshly written files). Exit code 0, no leftover process, the extraction folder is removed.",
                     "Unpacked/installed layout: window in about 0.4 s and engine ready in about 2.7 s when warm; the first launch after the build took 17.2 s to reach ready (cold file cache plus real-time scanning of unread files). Closing takes about 80 ms and leaves no process.",
                     "Against the 5 s cold-ready gate in the M8.1 contract: warm unpacked passes (2.6-2.8 s); first unpacked launch (17.2 s) and every portable launch fail.",
                     "The portable cost is dominated by self-extraction, which an installed or folder-based portable layout does not pay on each launch."
